{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And I, teragalti</b> — the tav of <b>תרגלתי</b> in place of heh, and there is none like it in Scripture. The meaning: I trained him to walk on his feet, just as a young child is trained when he is carried on arms — and this is like a remedy to strengthen the child until he can walk. And because Israel was compared to a trained calf, he said: <b>with cords of a man</b> — with ropes." "<b>I drew them with ropes</b> — love, not like the ropes that pull the plowing calf by the neck."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The lemma cites the ketiv form with tav; Ibn Ezra explains it as an anomalous conjugation substituting tav for heh."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:53.666192571Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}